  <data name="Preset_DialogBody1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>A preset is a checklist of "which mods to enable, and with which settings". A mod's own settings live in .OMniX_ModConfig.json inside its folder.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Preset_DialogBody2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Creating a preset records every currently enabled mod along with its settings. Applying it later enables exactly those mods and restores the settings to what they were.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Preset_DialogBody3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To let OMniX refresh 3Dmigoto for you, start Elevator first, then check "Auto-sync". Or do it yourself: check "Show manual controls", save / load settings by hand and press F10 to refresh 3Dmigoto.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Preset_DialogBody4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>You can also ignore presets entirely and just use the manual controls below to save mod settings.</value>
